    "result_text": "All 66 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, with both the new `Cp54Tests` (capacity warning) and the existing `Cp18Tests` (hard rejection at 50) green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `capacityWarning`, following the same stored-snapshot pattern as the existing `bulkSignupWarning` flag:\n\n1. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a `capacityWarning` (`capacity_warning`) boolean field with getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `capacity_warning` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/postgres as `BOOLEAN`, mysql as `BIT(1)`), positioned alongside `bulk_signup_warning`.\n\n3. **New step `AssignCapacityWarning`** \u2014 runs after `BuildOwner` (owner exists) and before `SaveOwner` (count excludes this owner). It counts owners in the same city (case-insensitive, matching `RejectCityAtCapacity`) and sets `capacityWarning = true` when the count is in `[40, 49]`, i.e. `>= 40 && < 50`.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `flagCapacityWarning` step into the pipeline between `flagBulkSignup` and `flagPossibleDuplicate`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` property to the owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it into the GET response.\n\nThe hard rejection at 50 (`RejectCityAtCapacity` throwing `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 409) is untouched, so an owner in a full city never reaches the warning step. The warning is a creation-time snapshot, consistent with how `bulkSignupWarning` and `possibleDuplicate` are described and stored.",
